      "procedure": "Procedure\nPreheat oven to 190°C. Grease a mini muffin tin with cooking spray.\nIn a medium bowl, whisk together the flour, cocoa powder, salt and baking powder.\nIn a large bowl, cream together the butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Beat in the egg and vanilla extract.\nGradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients, mixing until just combined. Stir in the chocolate chips.\nFill each muffin cup with about 2 tbsps. of dough. Press the dough up the sides of the cups to form a well. Bake for 10-12 minutes, or until the edges are firm.\nLet the cookie cups cool in the pan for 5 minutes, then transfer them to a wire rack to cool completely.\nHeat the cream in a saucepan over medium heat until simmering. Don't let it boil. Remove the pan from the heat, and add Lindt Swiss Milk Chocolate with Hazelnut. Let it sit for 3 minutes, then stir gently until the chocolate is melted and smooth. \nLet the ganache cool slightly before using. It will thicken as it cools.\nFill each cookie cups with a tablespoon of ganache. Top with strawberries, chopped hazelnuts and mint leaves."
