      "servingTime": "40 minutes",
      "yield": "4 servings",
      "tips": "",
      "ingredients": "Ingredients\nFOR THE VENETIAN SHRIMP:\n450g large shrimp, peeled and deveined\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n3 cloves garlic, minced\n1 tsp. red pepper flakes \n1 cup cherry tomatoes, halved\n1/2 cup Fiorelli Pinot Chardonnay\nSalt and black pepper to taste\n¼ cup parsley, chopped\nLemon wedges for garnish\nFOR THE POLENTA:\n1 cup polenta\n4 cups chicken broth\nSalt to taste\n1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese\n2 tbsps. unsalted butter",
      "procedure": "Procedure\nIn a saucepan, bring chicken broth to a boil. Mix in polenta and a pinch of salt. Stir constantly to avoid lumps. Reduce the heat to low and continue to cook, stirring frequently, until the polenta is thick and creamy.\nStir in the grated Parmesan cheese and butter. Adjust salt to taste. Keep warm.\nIn a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add minced garlic and red pepper flakes, then sauté for about 1 minute until fragrant. Add shrimp to the skillet, and cook for 2-3 minutes, or until they start to turn pink.\nPour in Fiorelli Pinot Chardonnay, and allow it to simmer for another 2-3 minutes, allowing the alcohol to evaporate and the flavors to meld.\nAdd halved cherry tomatoes to the skillet, and continue to cook until the tomatoes are slightly softened. Season with salt and black pepper to taste. \nTo serve, spoon the creamy polenta onto serving plates or a platter. Arrange the Venetian Shrimp and tomatoes over the polenta. Pour the Fiorelli Pinot Chardonnay sauce from the skillet. Garnish with fresh chopped parsley and lemon wedges."
